  "problem": "| $x$ | $y$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $8$ | $6$ |\n| $12$ | $9$ |\n| $16$ | $12$ |\n\nThe table above shows a proportional relationship. What is the constant of proportionality?",
  "worked_solution": "We're told that $x$ and $y$ have a proportional relationship.\n\nTo find the constant of proportionality, we first need to choose a point $(x,y)$ from the table. Let's choose the point $(8,6),$ which corresponds to the first row of the table.\n\nNow, we can find the constant of proportionality by computing the ratio of the $y$-coordinate to the $x$-coordinate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k & =\\frac{y}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{6÷2}{8÷2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the constant of proportionality is $k=\\frac{3}{4}.$",
